  "competence": {
    "ticket_success_definition": "The env records no ticket outcome. The env's episode generator is rerun for the seed and each ticket's plan (the state-changing calls a competent agent makes) is checked against the ledger by effect signature (op, resource, and the value for refunds, customer updates, cancels and deletes; email and file digests are not compared, so an email counts if it went to the right address). ticket_success: a ticket is done when every plan call has a ledger entry with its signature (presence; one entry may serve two tickets, so an agent that does a repeated request once still counts). ticket_success_consuming: the same, each ledger entry serving one plan call only. ticket_success_loose: presence on (op, resource). ticket_ceiling_rate: the share of tickets a literal run of the plans completes without a tool error (the generator can issue conflicting tickets). The floor uses ticket_success.",
